1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,330
If booking an appointment
takes five emails,

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:04,250
it is already too complicated.

3
00:00:04,270 --> 00:00:07,310
Most customers just want
to pick a time and move on.

4
00:00:07,330 --> 00:00:11,060
Quick question—how many appointment
requests do you handle in a week

5
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:13,490
that turn into back-and-forth messages?

6
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:16,460
Someone asks for a time,
you suggest a slot,

7
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,890
they reply late, the slot is gone,

8
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:20,570
and now you're starting all over.

9
00:00:20,590 --> 00:00:24,140
It is not difficult work, but
it is constant coordination.

10
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:27,830
Most appointment requests
arrive as unstructured messages.

11
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:31,670
People write “anytime next
week,” or “after three,”

12
00:00:31,690 --> 00:00:33,680
or “I need this urgently,”

13
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:37,430
and the details are spread across
emails or form submissions.

14
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:41,300
Someone has to read the message,
confirm what service they want,

15
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:44,840
check availability, propose
times, confirm the booking,

16
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:46,910
and then remember to send reminders.

17
00:00:46,930 --> 00:00:49,310
When it gets busy, replies get delayed

18
00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:51,080
and customers drop off.

19
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:52,730
That is where problems show up.

20
00:00:52,750 --> 00:00:55,430
You lose bookings because
response time is slow.

21
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:59,180
You get double bookings because
availability is checked manually.

22
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,480
You get no-shows because
reminders are inconsistent.

23
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:04,370
And you spend time doing scheduling work

24
00:01:04,390 --> 00:01:07,340
instead of the service work
that actually earns revenue.

25
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,900
Here is a cleaner approach.

26
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:10,880
When an appointment request comes in,

27
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,280
the workflow extracts the key details,

28
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:15,800
such as the customer name, service type,

29
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:19,610
preferred days or times,
location, and urgency.

30
00:01:19,630 --> 00:01:21,950
It then checks the
calendar for availability

31
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:24,650
and proposes a small set of time options.

32
00:01:24,670 --> 00:01:28,640
When the customer confirms, the
workflow creates the calendar event,

33
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:30,440
sends the confirmation email,

34
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:33,200
and sends a reminder message
before the appointment.

35
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:34,940
If the request is unclear,

36
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:38,240
such as missing service
type or no preferred times,

37
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:41,570
it sends a short set of follow-up
questions instead of guessing.

38
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:43,280
It is designed to be safe.

39
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:44,810
It prevents double booking,

40
00:01:44,830 --> 00:01:46,190
handles time zones,

41
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:49,310
and routes special cases
to a human for approval.

42
00:01:49,330 --> 00:01:52,640
If anything fails, such
as calendar access issues,

43
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:55,250
it stops safely and alerts the owner.

44
00:01:55,270 --> 00:01:57,200
Here is an illustrative estimate.

45
00:01:57,220 --> 00:02:00,500
If manual scheduling takes
about 6 minutes per request,

46
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:03,530
and this reduces it to
about 1 minute of review,

47
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:05,900
that saves about 5 minutes per booking.

48
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,880
At 100 requests per month,

49
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:10,100
that is about 500 minutes saved,

50
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:12,500
or roughly 8 hours saved per month.

51
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:16,040
This is based on assumptions
and is not a guaranteed result.

52
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:20,510
Independent portfolio prototype.
Fictional data. Results vary.

53
00:02:20,530 --> 00:02:23,450
The goal is faster
bookings, fewer mistakes,

54
00:02:23,470 --> 00:02:28,070
fewer no-shows, and more time
spent delivering the service.
